magic:
  type: "spell"
  spells_starting: 6
  spell_levels_allowed: [1, 2, 3]
  spells_per_level: 2
  spells_per_level_levels: up_to_character_level
natural_abilities:
  - { name: "Shadow Meld", description: "Shadow-meld at will, as the spell, for no P.P.E. Silhouettes are quasi-elemental beings of shadow and this is what they are, not something they cast." }
  - { name: "Absorb Light", description: "Drain the light in a 50 foot (15.2 m) radius by as much as 95 percent - near complete darkness." }
  - { name: "Strong in the Dark", description: "In shadow, darkness or at night a silhouette is +6 to P.S., +50 to M.D.C. and prowls at 85 percent. All of it goes away in normal light; see the vulnerabilities." }
  - { name: "Ley Line Powers", description: "A silhouette has ALL the special abilities of a ley line walker - line drifting, line phasing, line observation ball, sensing a rift, reading ley lines, and the rest. The book grants them by reference and prints none of them here." }
  - { name: "Low Supernatural Strength", description: "Physical strength is supernatural, on the low band. The sheet has no strength-type field." }
  - { name: "Horror Factor", description: "11. A number the silhouette projects, which the sheet has no field for." }
  - { name: "Average Life Span", description: "500 years." }
  - { name: "Size", description: "Five to six feet tall (1.5 to 1.8 m), 100 to 150 lbs (45 to 68 kg)." }
side_effects: "LIGHT TAKES EVERYTHING AWAY. In normal light a silhouette loses all its special bonuses - the +2 initiative, the +2 to strike, parry and dodge, the +4 to roll with impact, the +6 P.S., the +50 M.D.C. and the 85 percent prowl. In bright sunlight or under an intense spotlight it is worse: -2 to strike, parry and dodge, HALF its melee attacks and actions, and -10 M.D.C."
skills:
  occ_skills:
    - { name: "Language: Native Tongue", base: 98, per_level: 0, note: "The silhouette tongue, similar to the language of elementals, known by every silhouette at 98%." }
    - { choose: 2, from: ["Language: Other"], bonus: 15, note: "Two additional languages (+15%). The catalog''''s repeatable Language: Other row is what an any-language pick resolves through." }
  occ_related_skills:
    count: 18
    categories:
      - { name: "Communications", bonus: 10 }
      - { name: "Domestic", bonus: 5 }
      - "Electrical"
      - { name: "Espionage", bonus: 5 }
      - "Mechanical"
      - "Medical"
      - "Military"
      - "Physical"
      - "Pilot"
      - "Pilot Related"
      - { name: "Rogue", bonus: 10 }
      - "Science"
      - { name: "Technical", bonus: 10 }
      - "Weapon Proficiencies"
      - "Wilderness"
    note: "A silhouette has no basic skill program at all. Instead it selects EIGHTEEN skills from this list, which the book asks be chosen to fit the character''''s education and training. There is no schedule: eighteen at first level is all a silhouette gets. Technical is printed as Any (10%) with the plus sign dropped, which is a typesetting slip - every other entry in this list has one and the whole book prints these as bonuses."
  secondary_skills:
    count: 6
    note: "Six secondary skills from the same list, without the bonuses in parentheses, starting at the base skill level."
extraction_notes: |
  - Read from the OCR cache of a scan and verified against 200 dpi renders of
    printed 80 and 81, which between them carry the whole stat block and the
    whole skill list. The lore runs from printed 80 and both pages were read to
    the end.
  - ALMOST EVERY COMBAT BONUS THIS RACE HAS IS CONDITIONAL AND NONE OF THOSE IS
    STORED. The book prints "+2 on initiative, +2 to strike, parry and dodge, +4
    to roll with impact, BUT ONLY WHEN IN THE SHADOWS. +4 to save vs horror
    factor." `bonuses` is applied unconditionally, so only the horror factor
    save is in it; the rest are in `side_effects` and in the Strong in the Dark
    ability. A silhouette standing in daylight is an ordinary creature, and
    storing the shadow bonuses would have made it a good fighter everywhere.
  - THE SUNLIGHT PENALTIES ARE DISPLAY ONLY. `side_effects` is prose the sheet
    shows and nothing computes. Halving a character''''s melee attacks in bright
