  - MDC IS DERIVED FROM AN ATTRIBUTE. The book prints "P.E. plus 1D4x10 M.D.C.,
    plus 1D6 per level of experience", so the base is not a roll at all - it is
    a rolled attribute plus a roll. `mdc_base` is free text and carries it as
    printed; nothing adds it up. This is the same shape as the Zero Gravity
    Movement & Combat skill base filed as F2, in a different column.
  - LEY LINE POWERS BY REFERENCE. "Silhouettes have all the special abilities of
    ley line walkers" and the book prints not one of them. They are named in
    `natural_abilities` and left unenumerated, because inventing a list here
    would be writing rules rather than importing them - the ley line walker''''s
    own entry is in the main Rifts book.
  - THE SPELL SCHEDULE IS FULLY STORED, and it took a grep to find out. `magic`
    holds six spells from levels 1-3 at creation, then `spells_per_level: 2`
    with `spells_per_level_levels: up_to_character_level` for "an additional two
    spells per level of experience. New spells cannot exceed the character''''s
    current experience level." That is the LEY LINE WALKER''''S OWN RULE, named in
    the comment above `spellLevelsForGrant` in js/leveling.js, and this race is
    granted every ley line walker ability anyway. `frontmatter.md` lists four
    keys under `magic` and neither of these is among them - the reference is
    EXAMPLES, exactly as it is for save keys, and the draft first said the app
    could not express this. It can.
  - PSIONICS ARE "Standard; about the same as humans", so there is no psionics
    block and no `psionics_allowed`: the character rolls on the Random Psionics
    Table like anyone else. Absent and false are different statements and this
    book makes both, in different entries.
  - A RACE CARRIES NO xp_table. Printed 183 heads the column "Silhouette,
    Draconid & Repo-Bots"; composition is race-primary, so a table here would
    win over the occupation''''s and silently drop it. The ladder is: 0, 2,201,
    4,401, 9,001, 19,001, 28,001, 40,001, 60,001, 80,001, 100,001, 150,001,
    200,001, 275,001, 350,001, 425,001.
  - A natural M.D.C. creature, so there is no S.D.C. and no CORE_SDC_BY_CLASS
    entry.
  - The race states no Money, no Cybernetics and no standard equipment; all come
    from the O.C.C. if one is taken.
---

## Lore

The silhouette are jet-black humanoids with solid white eyes, otherwise very
human-looking - svelte, graceful, delicate-featured and, by human standards,
strikingly attractive. They are quasi-elemental beings of shadow: they can melt
into a shadow at will and drain the light out of a room. It makes them ideal
spies and assassins, and it has earned them the distrust of nearly everyone.

Their homeworld is beset by magic and Rifts, not unlike Rifts Earth, with two
differences: its nights run twenty hours out of a twenty-eight hour day, and
most of the Rifts there open onto the shadow dimension where the shadow beasts
live. Whether the silhouette evolved on that planet or came through from that
dimension, nobody knows.

## Conquered, and then promoted

The kreeghor took them several centuries ago. Before that the silhouette had
colonized a dozen planets with magic and Rift-drive technology, and the kreeghor
found shadowy shape-shifters suspicious enough that justifying a war was easy.
It took six years. A hundred years earlier the species would simply have been
exterminated; the wiser and gentler kreeghor of the day decided they were too
useful for that.

They were right. Under the Transgalactic Empire the silhouette have prospered.
They are an important part of the Imperial Army and hold serious positions in
government and industry. Some have joined the Freedom Fighters, though they have
to get past the suspicion of every other race first - and that suspicion is
frequently well earned, because a great many silhouette work for the Empire''s
Security Division and a fair number of those are trying to infiltrate the rebels.

## Outside the Empire

Silhouettes are scattered in small groups across a lot of planets and most of
the spaceways. The largest concentration outside the Empire is in the Warlock
Federation, where they are widely respected as mages, and there is another in
the Paradise Federation, where they work as security and as entertainers. The
rest turn up among pirates, mercenaries and adventurers.

## GM Notes

Available as a player character with the Game Master''s approval. Alignment: any.

The whole race is magical. A silhouette starts knowing six spells from levels
one to three and learns two more per level, never above its own level - and it
has every special ability a ley line walker has, which the book grants by
reference and does not print.

Read the light before reading the bonus line. In shadow a silhouette is +2 on
initiative, +2 to strike, parry and dodge, +4 to roll with impact, +6 P.S., +50
M.D.C. and prowls at 85%. In ordinary light all of that is simply gone. In
bright sunlight or under a spotlight it is -2 to strike, parry and dodge, loses
half its attacks, and is down 10 M.D.C. Only the +4 vs horror factor is on the
sheet, because only that one is always true.

They are respected but not befriended by the kreeghor and most other races.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'silhouette');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'silhouette';

